I was just playing a Tourist, and found an armor shop containing a few
weapons.  The best was a curved sword (probably slightly better than
+2 darts), and I decided to buy it (didn't feel like waiting for my
cat to steal it).

When I got out into the corridor, I looked at my inventory, and the
the curved sword was now a scimitar.  I checked through the source,
and sure enough, when you buy an ordinary weapon or armor (or blank 
scrolls but who cares) from a shopkeeper, the shopkeeper identifies 
them for you free of charge.

(Yes, this is the standard nethack 3.1.3)
